ame":"Noah.msi","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":7397376,"digest":"sha256:89d9a151633f0ddd34e129781f6bee770be60fe221fafae356515a11c28ab4f3","download_count":4,"created_at":"2026-07-03T12:40:32Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T12:40:32Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/noahapp/noah-for-tinkerers/releases/download/v2.0.0/Noah.msi"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/noahapp/noah-for-tinkerers/tarball/v2.0.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/noahapp/noah-for-tinkerers/zipball/v2.0.0","body":"**Noah for Tinkerers** is the open-source, bring-your-own-key build of Noah — a desktop agent that fixes your computer in plain English, with a safety harness around every action. You bring an Anthropic API key; Noah talks to Claude directly from your machine. No account, no backend.\n\n## Highlights\n\n- **Bring your own key, no backend** — your key stays on your machine; the only thing that leaves is the conversation with Claude.\n- **A real safety harness** — read-only diagnostics first, an explicit plan, approval gates on risky commands, and a hard-deny floor that permanently refuses catastrophic operations (wiping your home folder or keychains, erasing a disk) — even if asked. [How the harness works ›](https://github.com/noahapp/noah-for-tinkerers/blob/main/docs/design/3-safety-harness.md)\n- **Every command explains itself** — Noah can't propose a shell command without a plain-English reason, enforced at the schema level.\n- **26 playbooks** — Markdown remediation procedures (disk recovery, network diagnostics, printer repair, and more). Drop in your own; no rebuild, no plugin API.\n- **Monochrome, technical UI** and the wrench mark — the open build's own identity.\n- **AGPL-3.0**, built in public.\n\n## Install\n\n- **macOS** — `.dmg` (universal, Apple Silicon + Intel)\n- **Windows** — `.msi` / `.exe` (x64)\n- **Linux** — `.AppImage`\n\nThen open **Settings**, paste an `sk-ant-` key, and tell Noah what's broken. Don't trust a binary? Read every line or build it yourself — see [CONTRIBUTING](https://github.com/noahapp/noah-for-tinkerers/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n\nFull list in the [CHANGELOG](https://github.com/noahapp/noah-for-tinkerers/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md), and the engineering [design notes](https://github.com/noahapp/noah-for-tinkerers/tree/main/docs/design) go deep on how it's built.\n"}